{"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"All three items are implemented, tested, and committed.\n\n## 1. The envelope is now fully producer-blind\n\nannals' envelope carries zero downstream concepts: `actor` is gone, `producer` slimmed to `{tool, version?}`, and everything vocabulary-flavored (actor, source, model, provider, session_id) moved into a new **`meta`** field — arbitrary producer-owned metadata the store never interprets. And you were right that ids are the crux: with the envelope blind, each field reduces to two store-level questions — *in the id hash?* and *redaction-walked?* The README now has that table. `meta`'s answers are the design: **excluded from identity** (so provenance can be added or enriched later without the same fact getting a new id — the exact trap that forced cledger's old \"model can't join identity\" compromise) and **walked by redaction/scan** (metadata can leak secrets). A vocabulary that needs one of its facts *in* identity puts it in `content`. The new identity subset is just `{schema, kind, occurred_at, stream, media_type, content, links}`.\n\nThe satisfying part: **cledger's flat shape survived as a view.** Its `schema.ts` now owns `toAnnals`/`fromAnnals` translation — actor and producer-extras fold into `meta` on write and lift back on read (tolerating old ev1 lines too) — so the adapters, CLI, tests, and turnbridge didn't change by a single line. Verified on the wire: a stored note line is now `{producer: {tool}, meta: {actor, source, model, session_id}, …}`. The `source`/`model` read filters moved from annals into cledger's wrapper, where the vocabulary lives.\n\n## 2. Size policy: warn by default, refuse by opt-in\n\n`limits.warnEventBytes` (default 5MB — calibrated to your \"fits in a context window is fine\" line) warns on stderr but never blocks; `limits.maxEventBytes` is the opt-in hard refusal for producers that would rather fail loudly than replicate a blob, with a note that it should never be enabled on a capture path. Config-mergeable per repo/user, tested.\n\n## 3. Identity as first-class: documented as an optional pattern, not built\n\nSince `actor` left the envelope, the git-bug-style version needs no machinery at all: an identity is just a record like any other, and a turn claims authorship via `links: [{rel: \"authored_by\", target: <identity record id>}]`. The README documents that pattern next to the denormalized alternative (`meta.actor`, what cledger does today), and notes a vocabulary can migrate from one to the other without any envelope change. Nothing mandatory.\n\nState: annals 150/150, cledger 90/90, turnbridge 91/91 (zero changes needed there), end-to-end smoke re-run clean including the on-the-wire shape check. Commits: annals `b9dc00e`, conversation-ledger `d822870` on `annals-extraction`. Since your live install tracks the working directory, new captures are already writing the producer-blind shape — all pre-wipe, so the wipe script story is unchanged.\n\nresult: Envelope is now producer-blind (actor and AI-provenance fields moved to an identity-excluded, redaction-walked `meta`; cledger keeps its flat shape via a translation layer so adapters/CLI/turnbridge needed zero changes), size policy enforces softly at 5MB with opt-in hard cap, and identity-as-records is documented as an optional git-bug-style pattern — all suites and smoke tests green, committed on the existing branches.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"annals-extraction","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"d822870bf6a1f6bc481e56557deffd2045a36202","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-8854a57d4a329a100d0c4d97b956888642cbfc06c68d7f2f4e4bba96b9c7c3c7","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"id":"claude-fable-5","type":"agent"},"model":"claude-fable-5","session_id":"a044dbb5-5e38-4400-bb2a-97061ee33f87","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.263"},"occurred_at":"2026-09-07T23:51:55.694Z","producer":{"tool"